text:
tara: heads-up: spotted another confusing case for Go generator streams. When an auth refresh happens mid-stream and the app cancels the ctx the SDK sometimes leaves a reader goroutine stuck. Repro in sampleapp/generator/shutdown-repro.go. Anyone free to triage?

vik: yup, that's the ctx vs transport lifecycle mismatch. If the transport reconnects while the caller cancels the parent ctx you can end up with two goroutines racing to send to the events channel.

leo: short-term defensive pattern: stream should maintain an internal transportCtx separate from the user ctx. On auth failure set an "abandoned" flag and cancel transportCtx, but don't touch user ctx. That ensures Abort() semantics without surprising the caller.

tara: pasted minimal sketch below. The key is atomic state and not closing channels from two places.

```go
// internal
transportCtx, transportCancel := context.WithCancel(context.Background())
var abandoned atomic.Bool

go func() {
  defer transportCancel()
  for {
    select {
    case <-transportCtx.Done(): return
    case ev := <-recvCh:
      if abandoned.Load() { continue }
      outCh <- ev
    }
  }
}()

// on auth expiry
abandoned.Store(true)
transportCancel()
```

vik: SDK parity note: Node/Python have explicit Resume/Abort primitives. Go relying on ctx only leads to onboarding friction because users expect a single simple pattern. We should add Abort() to the Go GeneratorStream ASAP; Resume() we can add later with a resume token.

leo: also document that Resume may replay the last event and recommend apps persist a last-seen sequence id to dedupe. I'll add sequence_id to Event shape in the API spec.

ci-bot: :robot_face: nightly: generator_stream_shutdown_test flaky 4/10. Logs: https://ci/internal/stream-456.

tara: action items: leo -> api change for sequence_id; vik -> small PR to stop goroutine leak (internal transportCtx + abandoned flag); tara -> add sampleapp snippet and a short README note "ctx cancel vs Abort()"; I'll also coordinate a 15m sync with node/python owners to align resume token shape.

vik: will open PR today and add a unit test that simulates auth expiry + ctx cancel deterministically.

leo: thanks, adding a short example in sampleapp showing idempotent persistence keyed by sequence_id to avoid dupes on resume.

tara: nice work team, this should reduce onboarding surprises. :thumbsup:
